WEBVTT

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.990
Chiharu-chan! Goro-oniichan is home!

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:47.550
Hey, don't wake her up! I barely got her to fall asleep just now.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:48.970
And what? That's petty.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.570
Where's Mom?

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.250
She left to pick up Shingo.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:55.960
But seriously,

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:00.400
to actually defeat the Kaido main team...

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.220
To tell you the truth, I was surprised.{AMS: "beat" to "defeat"}

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.910
I guess.

00:02:31.390 --> 00:02:33.960
Regardless, that was a really tough game.{AMS: OG TL: That was a very hard game in any case!}

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.670
Oh yeah, by the way, Dad,

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.340
how's the transfer procedure for Mifune High going?

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:44.430
Yeah, it looks like the entrance exam for Mifune is in August.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.930
Oh, so it's in August.

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.030
Don't be so impatient.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:55.450
Students who transfer in the middle of the year can't participate in tournaments.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.950
In your case, you'll only be able to participate in the summer tournament of your third year.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.160
If you're aiming to make it to Koshien, that'll be your first and last chance.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.050
I'm fully aware of something like that.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:12.670
Speaking of which, there's something that worries me.{AMS: "makes me concerned" to "worries me"}

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:19.170
I wonder if Mifune's baseball team will accept you with open arms...

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.430
What?

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:22.680
It wouldn't be surprising.

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:26.730
Even if your former close friends,
Komori-kun and the rest, are there...

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:29.930
in the last summer of third year,
if a transfer student suddenly becomes the ace...

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:34.690
there might be some who won't be pleased.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:40.910
In the worst case scenario, the manager might refuse to let you join the baseball team.{AMS: added "scenario"}

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:45.700
Wouldn't it be better for you to go and confirm things? {AMS: "should be worth it to go and check-out?" to "would be with while to go and check-out?"}

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.930
There's no way something so ridiculous is true!

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:53.420
Seriously!?

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.580
That's right, that's right!

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.430
Speaking of which, the summer tournament preliminaries have started.{AMS: added "that", "had}

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:08.930
Ball!

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.430
They're playing, they're playing!

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.770
Out!

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.140
Now this looks like real baseball.{AMS: "it" to "this"}

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.750
What? 6-0!?{AMS: "Six to nothing" to "6-0"}

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:36.120
<i>Wait a minute, isn't Koyo the famous high school that's always in the top eight?{AMS: "always reaches the Best 8" to "that's always in the top eight" would have used quarterfinals normally but saying this means the same thing and means they could sometimes go higher}</i>

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:40.420
Third batter, first base: Oobayashi-kun.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.630
Oobayashi's the third batter?

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:45.430
Ball!

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.140
<i>Those pitches are pretty fast.</i>

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.430
<i>Mifune actually scored six runs on this pitcher...</i>

00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:57.950
Safe!

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:01.420
O-Oobayashi...

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:04.980
Fourth batter, catcher: Komori-kun.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:12.370
Do your best, Komori!

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.790
Yeah! He did it! Great!

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:25.190
{Missing tl?}{AMS: too faint}

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.970
<i>{eventually overlap, if we're to put anything at "missing tl" line above, sangofe}We used to lose in the first round every year; to think that we'd become this strong...</i>

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:31.680
<i>Even though they're only second-years, they're cleaning up.{AMS: "did a clean-up" to "they're cleaning up", "While" to "Even though"}</i>

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.330
Fifth batter, pitcher: Yamane-kun.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.060
<i>What?</i>

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.560
<i>Yamane is the pitcher?</i>

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.110
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:50.590
<i>Yamane couldn't even throw a ball with his left when fielding before.{AMS: "fielding ball" to "ball when fielding}</i>

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.890
Strike!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:03.840
Strike two!

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:07.800
<i>The guy who wasn't able to throw a ball further than 50 meters before...{AMS: "pitch" to "throw" added "before"}</i>

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.220
<i>How can it be!?</i>

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:14.620
<i>I'm not the only one.</i>

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:21.360
{I'm not the only one. Here also, there are people running on their tracks as fast as possible.}

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:21.360
<i>Here too, there're people who are running along their tracks as fast as possible with their own feet! {AMS: "on" to "along"}</i>

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:29.070
It seems like they don't need me.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:35.420
I can't take the ace number away from a man who overcame such a difficulty.{AMS: "revived after much difficulty" to "overcame such a difficulty" like goro}

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.410
It can't be helped!

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.860
Well, there's mountains of other high schools around.{AMS: added "of the world"}

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:48.720
I'm home!

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:56.930
I'm home.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.190
Welcome home.

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.110
Goro-oniichan, let's play a game! Pressure Fight!

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.080
Let's play!

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.950
But Dad has a game today, doesn't he?

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.250
Isn't it starting soon?

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.270
No, not yet. {AMS: "soon" to "early"}

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.220
Is that so?

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:17.170
That's right! {AMS: "I tell you" to "I'm sure"}

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:19.200
You started lying recently, so...

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.000
I'm not lying!

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.540
All right, let's play for a while then! {AMS: "a little" to "for a bit"}

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:24.420
Yeah! Game!

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:24.420
Let's go!

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:31.390
Too high... Ball four.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:32.230
Today, Shigeno isn't-

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.800
What's going on, Dad? Get a hold of yourself!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.650
{Missing tl.***}{too faint}

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:37.570
Goro...

00:07:38.950 --> 00:07:42.490
don't you have something to tell your mother?

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:43.980
Something?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:52.460
Hey, young man! I didn't even hear a single word from you about leaving Kaido for Mifune!

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.820
But didn't you hear about it from Dad?

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:58.450
Is something wrong? {AMS: "I did wrong" to "Did I do something wrong?"}

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.170
About that, the circumstances have changed at Mifune so I'm not going there.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:08.420
Instead, I went to Edawara High and got an enrollment form. Help me send it. {AMS: "took" to "got"}

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.640
The level required to pass their exam isn't too high,

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:15.430
and as long as we pay the tuition, it should be easy to get accepted.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:21.830
Wait-

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:23.580
What are you doing?

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.520
Dad is pitching right now!

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.660
"As long as we pay the tuition," it's fine!?

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:31.930
Stop joking around!

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:36.150
What do you take your father's hard-earned money for!?

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.830
It went through! To the right!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:41.910
Don't throw!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:41.910
Don't throw!

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:52.320
Your father is too kind so he didn't say anything to you,

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:55.730
but I'll tell you honestly, I'm not pleased.{AMS: "tell you" to "say", added "to you"}

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:58.890
T-Then, what should I do?{This isn't timed on stutter- here's the retiming}

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.890
It's your selfish decision, so earn your own school fees.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:10.360
Whichever high school you choose,
you have two months before you begin school.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.570
Get a part-time job between your studies and your training.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:15.860
Hey, it took a while!

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.570
Come here, Shigeno-kun!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.560
What's with this, "Hey, it took a while"?

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.770
You should say, "Sorry for the wait," right?

00:09:23.770 --> 00:09:27.330
Also, don't place the bowl so roughly, it's being rude to the customer!{AMS: added "being"}

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.720
Do it properly, please!

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.050
<i>What? He told me to be energetic and loud.</i>

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.800
What is this!?

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.900
There's a hair in here!

00:09:40.900 --> 00:09:43.530
It's true! It's disgusting!

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:46.890
How are you going to compensate me? I ate all of it!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:51.650
I-I'm really sorry. I'll reimburse you for the meal.{AMS: "pay you back" to "reimburse"}

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:54.460
What? Only for our meal?

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:57.400
After serving us something like that? That's pretty disrespectful!

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.930
I-I beg you, wait one minute!

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.910
{Yes, not timed on "are" intentionally -sangofe}This is strange.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:07.100
This hair is brown, isn't it?

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:11.920
None of the staff here have brown curly hair.

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:16.370
Oh, there is! You have brown curly hair! Could it be...

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.950
You're an interesting employee...

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:21.930
Are you by any chance suggesting that I put this hair in my bowl on purpose?

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.870
Of course!

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:28.640
If you're going to put up false charges you need to do better than that, you geezers.{AMS: "old" to "you"... old is connoted by "geezer"}

00:10:29.830 --> 00:10:31.450
This kid!

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:32.770
You want to get beat up!?{AMS: "be to "get"}

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.830
I'm sorry, valued customers!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:35.750
Please simmer down!

00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:37.580
I'll give you ten meal vouchers!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:45.870
Why was I fired after half a day when all I did...

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:48.550
was protect the law and order at work?{AMS: removed "where I".... unnecessary}

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:52.530
Earning a living isn't as easy as I thought.

00:10:57.270 --> 00:10:58.340
Yes?

00:10:58.340 --> 00:10:59.790
Goro?

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:05.770
Yeah, it's Goro-kun,
the dedicated young worker and serious student.

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.400
This isn't a good time to be making jokes.{AMS: OG TL: It's not a good time for making jokes.}

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.950
I just got a call from Edawara High.

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:11.850
Regarding my enrollment?

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.860
I got rejected!? How is that possible?

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:17.630
You'll wake Chiharu.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:21.080
Why did Edawara High reject me?

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.110
I don't know.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.910
I haven't even taken the test yet.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.840
Why did they reject me when they've only looked at my enrollment form!?{AMS: added "when they've", removed "by" after "only",}

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:35.630
They said they didn't want to bother with the enrollment of a problematic student.

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:38.460
Did you do anything at Kaido?{AMS: "in" to "at"}

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.150
This is a free fansub.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.150
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:59.010
You look well.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.890
I thought you'd be more depressed than this.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:03.800
I'm glad I was wrong.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.340
I'm not well at all!

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:08.760
Why the hell did Edawara High reject me!?

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:11.910
Isn't it because of Kaido? {AMS: "that related to" to "it because of"}

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:17.460
It's Egashira's work.

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:23.220
After hearing your story yesterday, I called Edawara to check on it.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.890
According to them,

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:30.290
Kaido's reply to the request of your school records was,

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:33.350
"If your school is going to accept Shigeno Goro as a student...

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:37.770
we will regard it as dishonest recruiting and bring the case to the Federation."{AMS: Note - the "Federation is the Japan High School Baseball Federation}

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:41.250
For dishonest recruiting?

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.820
That's bullshit!

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.650
There's no truth to it, how could they be sued?{AMS: "why would they be sued" to "how could they be sued", "nothing true about it" to "no truth to it"}

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.580
You don't seem to get it.

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:54.330
It doesn't matter if it's true or not.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:59.900
From the school's perspective,
they don't have any reason to accept the enrollment...{AMS: "all those troubles" to "them trouble", "For" to "From", "side" to "perspective"}

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:02.090
of someone they don't know at all,
and who might cause them trouble.{AMS: "all those troubles" to "them trouble", "For" to "From", "side" to "perspective"}

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:08.300
If they were to be sued,
their baseball team could be frozen.

00:13:08.770 --> 00:13:12.600
When they take this into consideration,
the school's best choice is to do nothing.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:19.610
That's Egashira's low and spiteful revenge against you for rejecting to become Kaido's star.{AMS: "mean" to "spiteful"}

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:24.970
So...

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:34.900
So that means whichever high school I go to, I can't play baseball?{AMS: "goes" to "go"}

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:41.050
Where are you going?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.710
I seriously can't let that idiot off this time!

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:46.470
I'm going to beat the shit out of that momma's boy!

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:51.360
If you do such a thing, with a violent record,
you won't be able to get into <i>any</i> high school!{AMS: "join" to "get into"}

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.580
That's exactly what Egashira is hoping for!

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:01.420
I'm sorry.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:04.660
If I had a little more power,

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:06.950
I wouldn't have let him do it.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:11.170
It's not your fault.

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:14.410
After all, you're also a victim of Egashira in a way.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.170
But...

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:20.040
What can I do?

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:23.620
If I can't transfer, forget defeating Kaido,

00:14:23.620 --> 00:14:25.480
I can't even continue playing baseball! {AMS: "to play" to "playing", "beat" to "defeat"}

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:28.550
There's only one way...

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:32.910
There's only one way to escape Egashira's evil plan.

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:37.200
But, it comes with a huge risk.

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:42.090
To you, who's aiming to defeat Kaido, it's a great risk. {AMS: "beat" to "defeat", "liability" to "risk"}

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.570
Do you think you can do it?

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:56.600
Yes, it's Egashira.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:15:02.270
I have Seishuu High on the line enquiring about the acceptance of Shigeno Goro.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:05.030
Okay, I'll take it, transfer it to me.

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:05.630
Okay.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:07.570
Hello?

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.050
Yes, that's right.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:13.770
His student record?

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:17.000
Very well, I'm sending it to you right now.

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:19.970
However,

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:23.330
about him joining your baseball team,

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:26.440
I've heard some bad rumors.{AMS: "his" to "him", removed "of"}

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:30.650
Huh? But... there's no baseball team at our high school.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:32.160
W-What did you say!? {AMS: "are you saying" to "did you say"}

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:35.940
No... Yes.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.430
T-That's right.

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:39.660
Yes, goodbye.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:45.670
<i>What in the world is going on?</i>

00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.670
W-What!?

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.420
You want to go to Seishuu,
where there isn't a baseball team!?{AMS: "which doesn't have" to "where there isn't"}

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:54.080
If you enter, how do you intend to play baseball?

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.670
That's obvious, isn't it?

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:58.930
I only have to gather members and create a baseball team.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:04.940
If you think about it, it'll cause less trouble this way compared to joining an existing team.

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:08.020
I understand...

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.910
but you should go to a high school where I have connections.

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:14.110
Over there, the threat of dishonest recruiting will-

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:15.170
It's okay, Dad.

00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:19.810
A situation like this was something that I was hoping for.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:20.790
What?

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:23.590
Also, if it's for defeating Kaido,

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:26.170
the bigger the obstacle, the more fired up I'll be. {AMS: "beating" to "defeating", "liability" to "the risk"}

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.880
So you don't have to worry about me,

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:34.100
I'll deal with my own problems.

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:40.390
To be a man of my word, I have to earn the school fees myself like Mom told me to.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.340
The other day...

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:53.540
He was so self-centered, and made such carefree remarks that I yelled at him to get a job.

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:57.140
But it's not that he's self-centered.

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:00.630
No matter what age he is, he'll always be baseball-centered.

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:04.880
That's for sure.

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:10.660
Both his father and step-father are like that.

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:55.440
I see...

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:59.930
We understand the details behind your application.{AMS: "motivation" to "situation"}

00:18:00.410 --> 00:18:06.180
Our school, formerly an all-girls school, became co-ed two years ago.

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:12.210
Today, we have 452 girls and 38 boys.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:16.830
There are still too few boys.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:22.570
Therefore, our sports program is opening its doors wider to recruit more students. {AMS: "and raise our athletes numbers" to "in the effort to raisee the number of athletes"}

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:27.750
Thus there is no problem for you,
coming from Kaido High School's sports program.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:30.420
However...

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:34.920
It's sad but this school can't meet your expectations.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:38.420
What? Why the- Why is that so?

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:43.300
Because it's physically impossible to create a baseball club here.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:47.810
Physically impossible?
But you just said there were 38 boys.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:51.250
In our school's day program, there are only seven boys.

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:55.900
The other 31 students are part of the evening program.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:00.860
No way!

00:19:02.060 --> 00:19:03.370
What!?

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.110
There's only seven boys?

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:12.880
Right. With me entering, it makes eight. Which means we're short one member to create a baseball team.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:15.010
Then what are you going to do?

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:17.040
Even though you've already earned your school fees,

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:20.090
since you were going for the sports program, you haven't really studied, right?

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:21.210
I'm going!

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:26.160
Next spring, there'll be newcomers, right?

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.890
I'll invite them to join the baseball team.

00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:33.650
Of course, I can't be sure they'll all agree to play baseball,

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.900
and I don't know what kind of baseball we'll be able to play with such a group.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:42.070
But if I were to use Dad's connections to enroll in a famous high school because of this...

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.910
leaving Kaido would be meaningless.

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:47.650
I'm going to Seishuu.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.660
Well, we'll see what happens!

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:53.620
Goro...

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:00.670
Don't worry, Mom.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:06.050
I haven't been this excited since Little League.

00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:17.270
I'm off!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:32.460
Morning! It's Fuji-kun!

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.260
Oh? Huh?

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:40.300
Wait a minute, Kaoru-chan!

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:44.050
We haven't seen each other since summer vacation began. Don't be so cold!

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.190
Hey, hey, hey-

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:51.540
Don't come any closer.
If you come any closer, I'm going to beat you up.{AMS: "nearer" to "any closer", "gonna" to "going to"}{even though this was a redone splitter}

00:20:56.830 --> 00:21:01.900
But why, when I'm shooting such lovey-dovey rays at you?

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:06.910
You're 17, with only softball as a lover, don't you feel lonely?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.660
What do you dislike about me?

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:13.410
I may look like this, but I'm pretty popular, you know!

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:15.870
Everything.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:21.220
I-It doesn't matter, you aren't seeing anyone else anyway,

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:23.420
or could it be that you already have someone you like?

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:24.920
There is.

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.890
Who exactly is this lucky guy?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:35.840
He must have smoother skin and tell better jokes than me, right?{AMS: removed "must" after "and"}

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:38.400
You really are a moron.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:44.400
I have no interest in a loser like you who spends all his free time doing nothing.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:48.850
At least the guy I know is totally different from you!

00:21:50.770 --> 00:21:52.910
He's a little stupid, but he loves baseball,

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.410
and he's betting his life to achieve his dream.

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:58.920
Right now, he's training, aiming for Koshien.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:03.670
So, we won't be able to see each other for a while, but...

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:16.680
Yo! You sure are getting intimate early in the morning, Shimizu.

00:22:17.800 --> 00:22:19.190
<i>Honda...</i>

00:22:19.540 --> 00:22:20.900
<i>Who's he?</i>

00:22:21.600 --> 00:22:24.070
H-Honda!? Why are you here?

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:25.930
"Why," you ask.

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:27.570
Yeah... Why?

00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:30.270
Firstly, I left Kaido.

00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:35.200
Secondly, I'm now a student at Seishuu.

00:22:36.900 --> 00:22:40.670
Thirdly, starting now, I'm taking the bus to school.

00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:43.280
It's... It's impossible!

00:22:42.890 --> 00:22:43.600
{Y-You're lying!}{AMS: all i hear is Honda going "Oh" here}

00:22:44.640 --> 00:22:49.180
Could you be one of the very few boys at Seishuu!?

00:22:50.240 --> 00:22:51.680
And what if I am-

00:22:52.680 --> 00:22:57.680
Congratulations! You've just been chosen to be the second member of Seishuu High baseball team!

00:22:58.140 --> 00:22:59.370
What?

00:24:41.660 --> 00:24:48.420
None of the seven male students I met at Seishuu High are interested in baseball!

00:24:48.420 --> 00:24:51.500
Hey, hey! Will I really be able to create a baseball team?

00:24:52.560 --> 00:24:53.670
Next time, on Major:

00:24:52.670 --> 00:24:54.960
{Next time, on Major: New Friends!}

00:24:53.670 --> 00:24:55.220
New Friends!

00:24:55.220 --> 00:24:57.590
Run to the stage of your dreams!
